---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import portrait from '../images/alex-portrait.jpeg';
import family from '../images/family.jpeg';
import otis from '../images/otis.jpeg';
import meredithAndFiru from '../images/meredith-and-firu.jpeg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Alex Partida is a web developer and designer in Los Angeles. Apparel production manager turned developer, three years on the web team of a daily newspaper, now building sites for small businesses and independent practitioners."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container about-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>I came to this work from running production floors.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Which turns out to be useful training for building things small
          businesses have to live with.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt="Alex Partida"
        class="portrait"
        widths={[320, 480, 640]}
        sizes="(max-width: 760px) 60vw, 320px"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Before I wrote software I was an apparel production manager in Los
          Angeles — schedules, vendors, margins, and the specific stress of a
          deadline that cannot move. I changed careers through a coding
          bootcamp and a web development certificate program at UC Davis
          Extension, and I have been building for the web professionally since
          2021.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm a web developer at <strong>The Salt Lake Tribune</strong>, a
          nonprofit daily newspaper, where I've been since 2021. I migrated
          their newsletter platform from Mailchimp to Iterable, build the
          subscription, donation and sponsorship features that fund the
          newsroom, and work on the bill tracker readers use to follow the Utah
          legislature. Shipping to an audience that notices the moment something
          breaks is a good education.
        </p>
        <p>
          Alongside that I take on a small number of freelance projects for
          small businesses and independent practitioners — a yoga teacher, a tax
          practice, people whose website is a real part of how they make a
          living rather than a brochure. Because I keep the list short, the work
          gets proper attention.
        </p>

        <h2>How the production background shows up</h2>
        <p>
          Running production teaches you that the handoff is the whole job. A
          beautiful sample means nothing if the factory can't reproduce it, and
          a beautiful website means nothing if its owner can't change the
          opening hours.
        </p>
        <p>
          So that's what I optimise for. When I built Christine's yoga site, the
          interesting decision wasn't the design — it was putting her class
          schedule in a Google Sheet she owns, so she posts her own dates from
          her phone without calling me. Every project ends with documentation
          written for the person who has to use it.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also care a lot about sites being fast and accessible, which is less
          a moral position than a practical one: a slow site on a phone on a bad
          connection is a site nobody reads.
        </p>

        <h2>Away from the keyboard</h2>
        <p>
          I live in Los Angeles with my partner Zach and my daughter Surie. We
          are outnumbered by animals — Otis the miniature poodle, Meredith Grey
          the Nebelung, and Firulais, who turned up on the patio one day, got
          fed once by my daughter, and never left. All three were adopted, two
          of them by accident.
        </p>
        <p>
          Weekends are horses, the piano in the living room, and all four of us
          reading completely different books in the same room. Learning to code
          changed my life in the obvious ways, and also in the one I didn't
          expect: I met Zach on the way through it. My daughter watches her mom
          work in a field without many women in it, which I think about more
          than I expected to.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="gallery">
        <figure>
          <Image
            src={family}
            alt="Alex with her family in Los Angeles"
            widths={[320, 560, 760]}
            sizes="(max-width: 760px) 90vw, 360px"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <Image
            src={otis}
            alt="Otis, a miniature poodle"
            widths={[320, 560]}
            sizes="(max-width: 760px) 44vw, 240px"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <Image
            src={meredithAndFiru}
            alt="Meredith Grey and Firulais, two rescued cats"
            widths={[320, 560]}
            sizes="(max-width: 760px) 44vw, 240px"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="cta__title">Working on something?</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        I'd like to hear about it — and I'll tell you straight if I'm not the
        right fit.
      </p>
      <div class="cluster cta__actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="/AlexPartidaResume.pdf" class="btn btn--ghost">Résumé (PDF)</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 5.5rem) 0;
  }

  .about-head {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .about-head > div {
    flex: 1 1 22rem;
  }

  .about-head h1 {
    margin-top: var(--s-2);
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .about-head .lede {
    margin-top: var(--s-3);
  }

  .portrait {
    width: min(320px, 60vw);
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    flex: none;
  }

  .gallery {
    margin-top: var(--s-5);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr));
  }

  .gallery figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .gallery img {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
  }

  .cta__title {
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .cta .lede {
    margin-top: var(--s-3);
  }

  .cta__actions {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }
</style>
